# NOTE: the editor forwards ONLY the GAMEKEY codes of its own instance keybinds (rpg-edit-hq-pchq/pieces/system/keybinds.pdl, untracked live data): arrows, space, b, g, m, 0-9 and Home work as is; n, r, PgUp, PgDn, End and BackSpace need `GAMEKEY` rows with codes 110, 114, 65365, 65366, 65367, 65288 added there (an owner decision, not done on the live editor); m (select next unit), g (random seed) and Home (backspace in the setup, north-west when playing) are the same functions on keys it already forwards.
# keys.pdl - what each key of civ-snes DOES (CONFIG; the driver holds no verb of its own). The camera keys Y U I O P belong to the board (D152): they are never bound here, and `l` (release) is the engine's.
# Key names are the GAMEKEY names of civ-snes-pchq/pieces/system/keybinds.pdl (name -> key code).
# KEYVERB | key | verb | arg      PLAY mode (a ledger exists): the verb page that key plays
KEYVERB | up        | move   | n
KEYVERB | down      | move   | s
KEYVERB | left      | move   | w
KEYVERB | right     | move   | e
KEYVERB | pgup      | move   | ne
KEYVERB | pgdn      | move   | se
KEYVERB | end       | move   | sw
KEYVERB | home      | move   | nw
KEYVERB | b         | found  | -
KEYVERB | 1         | build  | warrior
KEYVERB | 2         | build  | settler
KEYVERB | space     | endturn | -
KEYVERB | n         | select | next
KEYVERB | m         | select | next
# SETUPKEY | key | action | arg    SETUP mode (no ledger yet): the action of `civ_op setup`; space plays the `start` verb page (the NEW row); r = a random seed
SETUPKEY | up        | prev   | -
SETUPKEY | down      | next   | -
SETUPKEY | left      | dec    | -
SETUPKEY | right     | inc    | -
SETUPKEY | space     | start  | -
SETUPKEY | r         | random | -
SETUPKEY | g         | random | -
SETUPKEY | home      | back   | -
SETUPKEY | backspace | back   | -
SETUPKEY | 0         | digit  | 0
SETUPKEY | 1         | digit  | 1
SETUPKEY | 2         | digit  | 2
SETUPKEY | 3         | digit  | 3
SETUPKEY | 4         | digit  | 4
SETUPKEY | 5         | digit  | 5
SETUPKEY | 6         | digit  | 6
SETUPKEY | 7         | digit  | 7
SETUPKEY | 8         | digit  | 8
SETUPKEY | 9         | digit  | 9
# RULE rows: poll_ms = how often the driver looks at the relay file; idle_poll_ms = the same 3 s after the last key; step_ms = the shortest time between two moves (a held arrow repeats; a press inside it is dropped)
RULE | poll_ms | 50
RULE | idle_poll_ms | 120
RULE | step_ms | 100
